IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ap-dates`
IMPORT `ap-duties`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic), Part IV (family provision, ss 90-99A), with the s 3 definition of domestic
-- partner and the s 101 transitional rule.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in ap-seat.l4, which imports it and never restates a rule.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Part's own words say no ("eligible person means", "must not
-- make ... unless satisfied", "must be made before", "No action shall lie"); or NOTHING where the Part does not answer on the
-- facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Court's judgments (moral duty, adequate provision, dependency, "appropriate
-- to extend", "properly made") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Administration
-- and Probate Act 1958, Version No. 130 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part IV -- Family provision`

§§ `s 101 -- which deaths this Part IV governs`

-- s 101: the amendments made to Part IV by Part 2 of the Justice Legislation Amendment (Succession and Surrogacy) Act 2014
-- "apply in respect of the estate of any person who dies on or after the commencement of Part 2 of that Act". The endnotes
-- give the commencement as 1 January 2015 (No. 80/2014, "Ss 3-26 on 1.1.15").
`Part IV in this form governs deaths from` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2015

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 101 -- this Part IV governs the estate` `the day of death` IF
    NOT (`the day of death` `is before` `Part IV in this form governs deaths from`)

§§ `s 3 and s 90 -- definitions`

-- s 3(1): "domestic partner of a person who dies means a registered domestic partner or an unregistered domestic partner";
-- "unregistered domestic partner ... means a person (other than a registered domestic partner ...) who, although not married
-- to the person -- (a) was living with the person at the time of the person's death as a couple on a genuine domestic basis
-- (irrespective of gender); and (b) either -- (i) had lived with the person in that manner continuously for a period of at
-- least 2 years immediately before the person's death; or (ii) is the parent of a child of the person, being a child who was
-- under 18 years of age at the time of the person's death." "Registered" is a Relationships Act 2008 term: asked.
GIVEN `registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `living together as a couple at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `years lived together continuously before the death` IS A NUMBER
      `the parent of the deceased's child who was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a domestic partner` `registered` `living together as a couple at the death` `years lived together continuously before the death` `the parent of the deceased's child who was under 18` IF
        `registered`
    OR (    `living together as a couple at the death`
        AND (   `years lived together continuously before the death` AT LEAST 2
             OR `the parent of the deceased's child who was under 18`))

-- s 90: "disability means a disability -- (a) that is attributable to one or more intellectual, cognitive, neurological,
-- sensory or physical impairments or to one or more impairments attributable to a psychiatric condition; and (b) the
-- impairment or impairments are, or are likely to be, permanent; and (c) the impairment or impairments result in
-- substantially reduced functional capacity to undertake, or psychosocial functioning in undertaking, one or more of the
-- following activities -- (i) communication; (ii) social interaction; (iii) learning; (iv) mobility; (v) self-care;
-- (vi) self-management; and (d) the impairment or impairments affect the person's capacity for social or economic
-- participation".
DECLARE `Facts about a disability` HAS
    `attributable to an impairment of the kinds listed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permanent or likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `substantially reduces capacity in a listed activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `affects social or economic participation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about a disability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 90 -- a disability` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `attributable to an impairment of the kinds listed`
    AND `the facts`'s `permanent or likely to be permanent`
    AND `the facts`'s `substantially reduces capacity in a listed activity`
    AND `the facts`'s `affects social or economic participation`

DECLARE `My relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `the deceased's spouse at the death`
    `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner`
    `the deceased's child, including an adopted child`
    `the deceased's stepchild`
    `a person who believed the deceased was their parent and was treated as the deceased's natural child`
    `the deceased's former spouse or former domestic partner`
    `the deceased's registered caring partner`
    `the deceased's grandchild`
    `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Facts about me and the deceased` HAS
    `the relationship` IS A `My relationship to the deceased`
    `the day of the death` IS A DATE
    `registered domestic relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `living together as a couple at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years lived together continuously` IS A NUMBER
    `parent of the deceased's child under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at the death` IS A NUMBER
    `full-time student at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disability facts` IS A `Facts about a disability`
    `could have taken Family Law Act proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those proceedings were not taken or not finalised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `now prevented by the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deceased's child (my partner) has died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the deceased's child died` IS A DATE
    `a member of the deceased's household at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a past member likely to have become one again` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Eligible person` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
    `paragraph (b): a child under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or a child with a disability`
    `paragraph (c): a stepchild under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or with a disability`
    `paragraph (d): a person treated as a natural child, under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or with a disability`
    `paragraph (e): a former spouse or domestic partner prevented by the death from Family Law Act proceedings`
    `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
    `paragraph (g): any other person treated as a natural child`
    `paragraph (h): a registered caring partner`
    `paragraph (i): a grandchild`
    `paragraph (j): the spouse or domestic partner of a child who died within one year of the deceased`
    `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
    `not an eligible person`

-- s 90 "eligible person means -- (a) a person who was the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased at the time of the
-- deceased's death; (b) a child of the deceased, including a child adopted by the deceased who, at the time of the deceased's
-- death, was -- (i) under the age of 18 years; or (ii) a full-time student aged between 18 years and 25 years; or (iii) a child
-- with a disability; (c) a stepchild ... (the same three); (d) a person who, for a substantial period during the life of the
-- deceased, believed that the deceased was a parent of the person and was treated by the deceased as a natural child ... (the
-- same three); (e) a former spouse or former domestic partner of the deceased if the person, at the time of the deceased's
-- death -- (i) would have been able to take proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 ...; and (ii) has either -- (A) not taken
-- those proceedings; or (B) commenced but not finalised those proceedings; and (iii) is now prevented from taking or
-- finalising those proceedings because of the death of the deceased; (f) a child or stepchild of the deceased not referred to
-- in paragraph (b) or (c); (g) a person who [believed and was treated as in (d)] not referred to in paragraph (d); (h) a
-- registered caring partner of the deceased; (i) a grandchild of the deceased; (j) a spouse or domestic partner of a child of
-- the deceased ... if the child of the deceased dies within one year of the deceased's death; (k) a person who, at the time of
-- the deceased's death, is (or had been in the past and would have been likely in the near future, had the deceased not died,
-- to again become) a member of the household of which the deceased was also a member". A "means" definition: where no
-- paragraph holds, the answer is no. "aged between 18 years and 25 years" is read as 18 to 25 in whole years at the death,
-- both ends in (fork F8); "within one year of the deceased's death" as on or after the death and no later than one year after
-- it (fork F9). The first paragraph that holds is given; (k) is checked for every relationship that meets no earlier one.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about me and the deceased`
GIVETH AN `Eligible person`
`s 90 -- the kind of eligible person I am` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the relationship`
    WHEN `the deceased's spouse at the death` THEN `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
    WHEN `living with the deceased as a couple, or a registered domestic partner` THEN
        IF `s 3 -- a domestic partner` (`the facts`'s `registered domestic relationship`) (`the facts`'s `living together as a couple at the death`) (`the facts`'s `years lived together continuously`) (`the facts`'s `parent of the deceased's child under 18`)
        THEN `paragraph (a): the spouse or domestic partner at the death`
        ELSE `the household paragraph`
    WHEN `the deceased's child, including an adopted child` THEN
        IF `young, studying or disabled` THEN `paragraph (b): a child under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or a child with a disability` ELSE `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
    WHEN `the deceased's stepchild` THEN
        IF `young, studying or disabled` THEN `paragraph (c): a stepchild under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or with a disability` ELSE `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild`
    WHEN `a person who believed the deceased was their parent and was treated as the deceased's natural child` THEN
        IF `young, studying or disabled` THEN `paragraph (d): a person treated as a natural child, under 18, a full-time student aged 18 to 25, or with a disability` ELSE `paragraph (g): any other person treated as a natural child`
    WHEN `the deceased's former spouse or former domestic partner` THEN
        IF     `the facts`'s `could have taken Family Law Act proceedings`
           AND `the facts`'s `those proceedings were not taken or not finalised`
           AND `the facts`'s `now prevented by the death`
        THEN `paragraph (e): a former spouse or domestic partner prevented by the death from Family Law Act proceedings`
        ELSE `the household paragraph`
    WHEN `the deceased's registered caring partner` THEN `paragraph (h): a registered caring partner`
    WHEN `the deceased's grandchild` THEN `paragraph (i): a grandchild`
    WHEN `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased's child` THEN
        IF     `the facts`'s `the deceased's child (my partner) has died`
           AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the day the deceased's child died` `is before` `the facts`'s `the day of the death`))
           AND (`the facts`'s `the day the deceased's child died` `is on or before` (`the date` 12 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day of the death`)))
        THEN `paragraph (j): the spouse or domestic partner of a child who died within one year of the deceased`
        ELSE `the household paragraph`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN `the household paragraph`
    WHERE
        `young, studying or disabled` MEANS
               `the facts`'s `age at the death` LESS THAN 18
            OR (    `the facts`'s `full-time student at the death`
                AND `the facts`'s `age at the death` AT LEAST 18
                AND `the facts`'s `age at the death` AT MOST 25)
            OR `s 90 -- a disability` (`the facts`'s `disability facts`)
        `the household paragraph` MEANS
            IF    `the facts`'s `a member of the deceased's household at the death`
               OR `the facts`'s `a past member likely to have become one again`
            THEN `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household`
            ELSE `not an eligible person`

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Eligible person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 91 -- one of paragraphs (h) to (k)` `the kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `paragraph (h): a registered caring partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paragraph (i): a grandchild` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paragraph (j): the spouse or domestic partner of a child who died within one year of the deceased` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paragraph (k): a member of the deceased's household` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Eligible person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 91 -- paragraph (f) or (g)` `the kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `paragraph (f): any other child or stepchild` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paragraph (g): any other person treated as a natural child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 90A, 91 -- may the Court make a family provision order for me`

-- s 90A(1), (2): an eligible person may apply, within the time in s 99. s 91(2): "The Court must not make a family provision
-- order ... unless satisfied -- (a) that the person is an eligible person; and (b) in the case of a person referred to in
-- paragraphs (h) to (k) ..., that the person was wholly or partly dependent on the deceased for the eligible person's proper
-- maintenance and support; and (c) that, at the time of death, the deceased had a moral duty to provide for the eligible
-- person's proper maintenance and support; and (d) that the distribution of the deceased's estate fails to make adequate
-- provision for the proper maintenance and support of the eligible person, whether by -- (i) the deceased's will (if any); or
-- (ii) the operation of Part IA; or (iii) both". (3): for (2)(b) "the Court must disregard any means-tested government
-- benefits". The Court's satisfaction is asked; where every condition is met the Court MAY make an order (s 91(1)).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about me and the deceased`
      `I was wholly or partly dependent on the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased had a moral duty to provide for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate fails to make adequate provision for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my application is in time or the time is extended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91 -- the Court may make a family provision order for me` `the facts` `I was wholly or partly dependent on the deceased` `the deceased had a moral duty to provide for me` `the estate fails to make adequate provision for me` `my application is in time or the time is extended` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`s 101 -- this Part IV governs the estate` (`the facts`'s `the day of the death`)) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: s 101 leaves deaths before 1 January 2015 to Part IV as it was)
           IF `the kind` EQUALS `not an eligible person` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `my application is in time or the time is extended` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (`s 91 -- one of paragraphs (h) to (k)` `the kind`) AND (NOT `I was wholly or partly dependent on the deceased`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `the deceased had a moral duty to provide for me` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `the estate fails to make adequate provision for me` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the kind` MEANS `s 90 -- the kind of eligible person I am` `the facts`

DECLARE `What the Court must weigh or keep to` IS ONE OF
    `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`
    `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`
    `the degree to which I cannot provide adequately for myself by reasonable means (s 91(4)(c))`
    `the degree of my dependency on the deceased at the death (s 91(4)(d))`
    `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`
    `proportionate to my degree of dependency on the deceased at the death (s 91(5)(b))`

-- s 91(4), (5): what the Court must take into account in fixing the amount, and the two limits on it.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about me and the deceased`
GIVETH A LIST OF `What the Court must weigh or keep to`
`s 91(4), (5) -- what the Court must weigh, and the limits on my provision` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the kind` EQUALS `not an eligible person`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `s 91 -- paragraph (f) or (g)` `the kind`
         THEN LIST `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`, `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`, `the degree to which I cannot provide adequately for myself by reasonable means (s 91(4)(c))`, `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`
         ELSE IF `s 91 -- one of paragraphs (h) to (k)` `the kind`
              THEN LIST `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`, `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`, `the degree of my dependency on the deceased at the death (s 91(4)(d))`, `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`, `proportionate to my degree of dependency on the deceased at the death (s 91(5)(b))`
              ELSE LIST `the degree of the deceased's moral duty to provide for me (s 91(4)(a))`, `the degree to which the estate fails to provide adequately for me (s 91(4)(b))`, `no more than is necessary for my proper maintenance and support (s 91(5)(a))`
    WHERE
        `the kind` MEANS `s 90 -- the kind of eligible person I am` `the facts`

§§ `s 99 -- the time for applying`

-- s 99(1): "within 6 months after the date of the grant of probate of the will or of letters of administration" (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 99(1) -- my last day to apply` `the day of the grant` MEANS `the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the grant`

DECLARE `My family provision application` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `still open: apply by the last day`
    `late: it can go ahead only if the Court extends the period`
    `late, but the Court has extended the period`
    `late, and the period can no longer be extended, as the estate has been finally distributed`

-- s 99(2): "the Court may extend the period ... including in any case where the time for making an application has already
-- expired." (3): "An application for extension under subsection (2) must be made before the final distribution of the
-- estate."
GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the Court has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate was finally distributed before I sought an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My family provision application`
`s 99 -- where my application stands` `the day of the grant` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` `the Court has extended the period` `the estate was finally distributed before I sought an extension` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome of` (`s 99 -- the eligible person must apply within six months of the grant` (`the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` (`s 99(1) -- my last day to apply` `the day of the grant`))) `by` `the claimant` `with` `apply for a family provision order` `counted from` `the day of the grant` `done` `I have applied` `on` `the day I applied` `today`
    WHEN `done in time` THEN `in time`
    WHEN `still open` THEN `still open: apply by the last day`
    WHEN `not done in time` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the Court has extended the period` THEN `late, but the Court has extended the period`
               IF `the estate was finally distributed before I sought an extension` THEN `late, and the period can no longer be extended, as the estate has been finally distributed`
               OTHERWISE `late: it can go ahead only if the Court extends the period`

§§ `s 99A -- distributions the claim cannot disturb`

-- s 99A(4): a notice of intention to apply "(a) must be in writing signed by the eligible person or the eligible person's
-- legal practitioner; and (b) lapses within 3 months from the receipt of the notice by the personal representative unless an
-- application for a family provision order has been made to the Court; and (c) is incapable of being renewed."
GIVEN `the day the personal representative received my notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 99A(4) -- the last day before my notice of intention lapses` `the day the personal representative received my notice` MEANS
    `the date` 3 `months after` `the day the personal representative received my notice`

-- s 99A(1): "No action shall lie against the personal representative by reason of the personal representative having
-- distributed any part of the estate, and no application or family provision order shall disturb the distribution, if it was
-- properly made ... for the purpose of providing for the maintenance support or education of the partner or any child of the
-- deceased totally or partially dependent on the deceased". (2): no proceeding by a person who, "being of full legal capacity",
-- notified the personal representative in writing that they consent to the distribution or do not intend to apply. (3): no
-- action where the distribution "was properly made ... after the expiry of 6 months after the grant ... and either -- (a) the
-- personal representative has not had notice of an application ...; or (b) if the personal representative has had a notice of
-- an intention to make an application ... in accordance with subsection (4), the personal representative has not received
-- written notice that an application ... has been made to the Court within 3 months of the receipt of that notice". A flat
-- negative: JUST FALSE where a subsection holds; where none does, the section is silent (NOTHING).
DECLARE `Facts about a distribution` HAS
    `the distribution was properly made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was for the maintenance, support or education of the partner or a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had notified in writing my consent or that I would not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
    `the day of the distribution` IS A DATE
    `the personal representative had notice of an application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave a notice of intention to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the personal representative received my notice` IS A DATE
    `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I applied` IS A DATE
    `the personal representative received written notice of my application` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about a distribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99A -- I may proceed against the personal representative over the distribution` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the facts`'s `the distribution was properly made` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 99A protects only a distribution properly made)
           IF `the facts`'s `it was for the maintenance, support or education of the partner or a dependent child` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the facts`'s `I had notified in writing my consent or that I would not apply` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `after six months` AND (`no notice of an application` OR `the notice of intention lapsed`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 99A says when no action lies, not when one does)
    WHERE
        `after six months` MEANS `the facts`'s `the day of the distribution` `is after` (`the date` 6 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day of the grant`))
        `no notice of an application` MEANS NOT (`the facts`'s `the personal representative had notice of an application`)
        `the notice of intention lapsed` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `I gave a notice of intention to apply`
            AND (NOT (    `the facts`'s `I have applied`
                      AND (`the facts`'s `the day I applied` `is on or before` (`s 99A(4) -- the last day before my notice of intention lapses` (`the facts`'s `the day the personal representative received my notice`)))
                      AND `the facts`'s `the personal representative received written notice of my application`))
